{"summary":"The PR introduces a ProfileHeader component that computes a full name via useEffect and state instead of deriving it directly from props. This adds unnecessary component renders and state synchronization overhead.","rating":"needs-improvement","readiness":"changes-required","strengths":["Clean and readable component structure."],"assumptions":["No specific team rules or linter findings were provided, relying on standard React best practices."],"findings":[{"file":"src/features/profile/ProfileHeader.tsx","line":6,"endLine":10,"evidence":"  const [fullName, setFullName] = useState("");","title":"Store derived state in local variable instead of useState and useEffect","why":"Storing derived data in state and synchronizing it via useEffect causes extra renders and goes against React best practices. The full name can be directly derived during render from firstName and lastName.","fix":"Compute the full name directly in the render body without using useState or useEffect.","suggestedCode":"export function ProfileHeader({ firstName, lastName }: Props) {
  const fullName = `${firstName} ${lastName}`;
  return <h1>{fullName}</h1>;
}","category":"react","kind":"bug","severity":"medium","confidence":0.99}]}

