{"summary":"The PR introduces an AnnouncementCard component that renders raw HTML content using dangerouslySetInnerHTML without prior sanitization.","rating":"major-issues","readiness":"changes-required","strengths":["Clean and straightforward component structure."],"assumptions":["The bodyHtml string is not sanitized elsewhere before being passed into AnnouncementCard.","Employees who write announcements have permissions that could potentially allow Stored XSS vectors if malicious scripts are introduced."],"findings":[{"file":"src/features/announcements/AnnouncementCard.tsx","line":8,"endLine":8,"evidence":"      <div dangerouslySetInnerHTML={{ __html: bodyHtml }} />","title":"Unsanitized dangerouslySetInnerHTML introduces XSS risk","why":"Rendering raw HTML via dangerouslySetInnerHTML without sanitizing it first allows any malicious script present in bodyHtml to execute in the user's browser, leading to potential session hijacking or data theft.","fix":"Sanitize the HTML string using a robust library like DOMPurify before passing it to dangerouslySetInnerHTML.","suggestedCode":"import DOMPurify from 'dompurify';

export function AnnouncementCard({ title, bodyHtml }: Props) {
  const sanitizedHtml = DOMPurify.sanitize(bodyHtml);
  return (
    <article>
      <h2>{title}</h2>
      <div dangerouslySetInnerHTML={{ __html: sanitizedHtml }} />
    </article>
  );
}","category":"security","kind":"bug","severity":"critical","confidence":0.95}]}

{"summary":"The PR introduces an AchievementsPage component that fetches data via RTK Query and synchronizes it into a Redux slice using an effect, while also displaying an unhandled loading and error state.","rating":"needs-improvement","readiness":"changes-required","strengths":["Leverages RTK Query for data fetching hooks."],"assumptions":["selectAchievements reads from the Redux store slice that is being synchronized."],"findings":[{"file":"src/features/achievements/AchievementsPage.tsx","line":12,"endLine":15,"evidence":"  useEffect(() => {","title":"Duplicating server state into Redux store","why":"Copying RTK Query server data into Redux state via an effect duplicates state and bypasses the built-in caching, refetching, and loading state management provided by RTK Query.","fix":"Remove the redundant Redux slice state and useSelector, and pass the RTK Query data directly to the presentation component, handling loading and error states.","suggestedCode":"export function AchievementsPage() {
  const { data: achievements = [], isLoading, error } = useGetAchievementsQuery();

  if (isLoading) return <div>Loading...</div>;
  if (error) return <div>Failed to load achievements</div>;

  return <AchievementList items={achievements} />;
}","category":"state-management","kind":"bug","severity":"high","confidence":0.95}]}

{"summary":"The PR introduces an AchievementsPage component that fetches data using RTK Query and synchronizes it into Redux state via an effect. This duplicates server state into the Redux store unnecessarily, creating redundant state and boilerplate.","rating":"needs-improvement","readiness":"changes-required","strengths":["Clean component structure using feature-based modularity","Proper use of RTK Query hook for data fetching"],"assumptions":["The selectAchievements selector reads from a slice that duplicates data already available in the RTK Query cache."],"findings":[{"file":"src/features/achievements/AchievementsPage.tsx","line":12,"endLine":15,"evidence":"  useEffect(() => {","title":"Do not copy RTK Query server state into Redux store","why":"Copying server data into local Redux state duplicates state, causes unnecessary re-renders, and defeats the caching and automated invalidation benefits of RTK Query.","fix":"Remove the useEffect and Redux slice storage for achievements, and consume the RTK Query data directly in the component or pass it down.","suggestedCode":"export function AchievementsPage() {
  const { data: achievements = [] } = useGetAchievementsQuery();
  return <AchievementList items={achievements} />;
}","category":"state-management","kind":"improvement","severity":"medium","confidence":0.95}]}

{"summary":"Introduces a custom useWindowWidth hook to track window dimensions via window resize events.","rating":"needs-improvement","readiness":"changes-required","strengths":["Clean and straightforward custom hook structure."],"assumptions":["SSR is not used, or window is guaranteed to be defined when the hook executes."],"findings":[{"file":"src/hooks/useWindowWidth.ts","line":9,"endLine":9,"evidence":"  }, []);","title":"Missing event listener cleanup","why":"The resize event listener is added when the component mounts, but it is never removed during cleanup. This leaks memory and retains component state references if the component unmounts.","fix":"Return a cleanup function from useEffect that removes the resize event listener.","suggestedCode":"  useEffect(() => {
    const onResize = () => setWidth(window.innerWidth);
    window.addEventListener("resize", onResize);
    return () => window.removeEventListener("resize", onResize);
  }, []);","category":"react","kind":"bug","severity":"medium","confidence":1}]}

{"summary":"This pull request introduces a custom useWindowWidth hook to track window dimensions. However, it lacks a window resize event listener cleanup function, leading to a memory leak.","rating":"needs-improvement","readiness":"changes-required","strengths":["Simple and clean custom hook structure for tracking window dimensions."],"assumptions":["The code is intended for client-side execution in a browser environment."],"findings":[{"file":"src/hooks/useWindowWidth.ts","line":9,"endLine":9,"evidence":"  }, []);","title":"Missing event listener cleanup","why":"The useEffect adds a resize event listener to the window but fails to remove it in a cleanup function. Every time components using this hook mount, leaked event listeners accumulate and stay in memory.","fix":"Return a cleanup function from useEffect that calls window.removeEventListener.","suggestedCode":"  useEffect(() => {
    const onResize = () => setWidth(window.innerWidth);
    window.addEventListener("resize", onResize);
    return () => window.removeEventListener("resize", onResize);
  }, []);","category":"react","kind":"bug","severity":"medium","confidence":1}]}

{"summary":"The PR introduces a LeaveRequestForm component to submit leave requests using local component state and a direct API utility call. However, it lacks error handling, loading states during submission, and proper project state management integration with RTK Query.","rating":"needs-improvement","readiness":"changes-required","strengths":["Uses semantic form elements with proper label association.","Provides a status region for submission feedback."],"assumptions":["Project context specifies Redux Toolkit and RTK Query, but this form bypasses it for a direct API call."],"findings":[{"file":"src/features/leave/LeaveRequestForm.tsx","line":10,"endLine":10,"evidence":"    await submitLeaveRequest({ reason });","title":"Missing error handling on async form submission","why":"If submitLeaveRequest fails or throws an exception, the promise rejects unhandled, leaving the user without any error feedback and potentially breaking the UI flow.","fix":"Wrap the submission call in a try/catch block to handle errors gracefully and display an error message to the user.","suggestedCode":"    try {
      await submitLeaveRequest({ reason });
      setMessage("Leave request sent.");
    } catch {
      setMessage("Failed to send leave request.");
    }","category":"api","kind":"bug","severity":"high","confidence":0.95},{"file":"src/features/leave/LeaveRequestForm.tsx","line":18,"endLine":18,"evidence":"      <button type="submit">Send request</button>","title":"Missing loading state and button disable during submission","why":"The submit button is not disabled while the asynchronous request is in flight, allowing users to spam-click and submit duplicate leave requests.","fix":"Introduce an isSubmitting state to disable the button and change button text while the request is pending.","category":"correctness","kind":"risk","severity":"medium","confidence":0.9}]}

