}","category":"api","kind":"bug","severity":"high","confidence":0.95},{"file":"src/features/leave/LeaveRequestForm.tsx","line":18,"endLine":18,"evidence":"      <button type="submit">Send request</button>","title":"Missing loading state during submission","why":"The submit button remains interactive while the request is in flight, allowing the user to click multiple times and send duplicate requests.","fix":"Track the loading state during submission and disable the button while the request is pending.","category":"correctness","kind":"risk","severity":"medium","confidence":0.9}]}

{"summary":"The PR introduces a SaveEntryButton component utilizing RTK Query to update a timesheet entry and manages local success feedback via component state. A key missing error handling element leaves the UI unaware of failed update requests.","rating":"acceptable","readiness":"ready-with-minor-changes","strengths":["Disabled state properly bound to isLoading to prevent concurrent requests","Appropriate use of role=status for the success message to aid accessibility"],"assumptions":["RTK Query mutation returns a result object whose error can be checked or unwrapped."],"findings":[{"file":"src/features/timesheet/SaveEntryButton.tsx","line":10,"endLine":12,"evidence":"    await updateEntry(entry);","title":"Unhandled mutation error in SaveEntryButton","why":"If the updateEntry API call fails, the mutation promise may reject or return an error object. Currently, the code proceeds directly to setSaved(true) regardless of whether the save operation succeeded or failed.","fix":"Check the result of the mutation before setting the saved state, or handle potential errors gracefully.","suggestedCode":"    const result = await updateEntry(entry);
    if (!('error' in result)) {
      setSaved(true);
    }","category":"api","kind":"bug","severity":"high","confidence":0.9}]}

{"summary":"The PR introduces a SaveEntryButton component that triggers an RTK Query mutation. It lacks error handling for the mutation and does not reset the saved status on subsequent edits.","rating":"acceptable","readiness":"ready-with-minor-changes","strengths":["Uses semantic role="status" for announcing the saved state.","Disables the button while the mutation is in progress."],"assumptions":["The mutation returns a result object that can be checked for errors."],"findings":[{"file":"src/features/timesheet/SaveEntryButton.tsx","line":10,"endLine":10,"evidence":"    await updateEntry(entry);","title":"Missing mutation error handling","why":"If the network request fails, updateEntry will reject or return an error object, yet the code proceeds immediately to setSaved(true) without checking the result.","fix":"Check the result of updateEntry or unwrap it inside a try/catch block before setting the saved state.","suggestedCode":"  async function handleSave() {
    try {
      await updateEntry(entry).unwrap();
      setSaved(true);
    } catch {
      // handle error
    }
  }","category":"api","kind":"bug","severity":"medium","confidence":0.9}]}

